+  "overview": "Before this change a failed delivery was `nack`ed straight back onto the queue and a cron job re-sent everything from the last hour every 5 minutes. Now the consumer hands failures to a **retry scheduler** that uses the queue's delayed publish, and deliveries that exhaust their retries become visible (and replayable) to operators. Read the scheduler first: everything else hangs off it.",
